.TH PF 1 "2026" "Panefile @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pf \- keyboard-driven, multi-panel file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pf
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Panefile
is a file manager for Wayland in which one window contains any number of
independent directory panels side by side. Each panel keeps its own working
directory, cursor, history, sort order and filter. Panels are created, split,
closed and cycled with single keystrokes, and files are copied between them
without opening a second window.
.PP
Every action is reachable from the keyboard. The mouse is supported but never
required.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATH
A file or directory, absolute or relative, or a
.B file://
URI. Relative paths resolve against the working directory of the calling
shell, not that of any already-running instance. A path naming a file
navigates to its parent directory and places the cursor on the file.
.PP
Where a path opens depends on whether a Panefile window already has focus: if
it does, the focused panel navigates there; if it does not, the path opens in a
new panel and the window is raised. With several paths, the first follows that
rule and the rest each open a new panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Placement
.TP
.B \-\-here
Use the focused panel even when the window is not focused.
.TP
.B \-\-panel
Always open a new panel, even when the window is focused.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window in the existing process.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-instance
Start a separate process, ignoring any running instance.
.SS Default file manager (Linux)
.TP
.B \-\-make\-default
Make Panefile the default file manager, then exit. Sets
.B inode/directory
to
.B panefile.desktop
in
.BR mimeapps.list ,
editing the file that currently decides it and keeping a symlinked one a
symlink, and writes
.I ~/.local/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.FileManager1.service
so that \(lqShow in folder\(rq in browsers and other applications starts
Panefile. Exits non-zero, saying why, if either could not be done.
.TP
.B \-\-default\-status
Print the current
.B inode/directory
handler and the file that set it, whether the FileManager1 service file exists
and what it runs, and which process owns
.B org.freedesktop.FileManager1
on the session bus, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dbus\-service
Run as the
.B org.freedesktop.FileManager1
service. Started by the session bus through the service file
.B \-\-make\-default
writes, rather than by hand. Opens no window until a request arrives, and
exits after about ten seconds if none does; otherwise it behaves like any other
Panefile window. If Panefile is already running, requests are passed to it.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B \-\-startup\-trace
Print the timing of each startup phase to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-quit\-after\-paint
Exit as soon as the first frame has been painted. Intended for benchmarking.
.TP
.BI \-\-benchmark " DIR"
Scan
.I DIR
, print timings, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable
.B panefile.*
debug logging.
.SS Information
.TP
.B \-\-config\-dir
Print the configuration directory and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-default\-config
Print the default
.B config.toml
and exit. Redirect it into the configuration directory to start from a
complete, commented template.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/panefile/config.toml
Behaviour settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/panefile/hotkeys.toml
Key bindings. Every action may have any number of bindings, and a binding
containing spaces is a sequence of chords pressed in order.
.TP
.I ~/.config/panefile/theme.toml
Active theme name, or inline colour overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.config/panefile/themes/
User themes. Bundled themes live in
.IR @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR@/panefile/themes/ .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/panefile/
Pinned directories, session state and window geometry.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash/
The wastebasket, shared with the rest of the desktop.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mimeapps.list
The default application for each file type, including folders
.RB ( inode/directory ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.FileManager1.service
Written by
.BR \-\-make\-default .
Delete it to hand \(lqShow in folder\(rq back to the system's file manager.
.PP
On macOS these live under
.I ~/Library/Application Support/panefile/
instead, the cache under
.IR ~/Library/Caches/panefile/ ,
and the wastebasket is Finder's
.IR ~/.Trash .
All of them honour the
.BR PANEFILE_CONFIG_DIR ", " PANEFILE_STATE_DIR ", " PANEFILE_CACHE_DIR " and " PANEFILE_TRASH_DIR
environment variables.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor launched by
.BR e " and " E .
Falls back to
.BR VISUAL ", then " nano .
.TP
.B TERMINAL
Terminal emulator launched by
.BR T .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
.B \-\-make\-default
could not make Panefile the default file manager.
.TP
.B 2
A path argument did not exist, or an option was not recognised.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1)
.PP
Full documentation: @PROJECT_HOMEPAGE_URL@
